CLI Digital Clock (C) -
A simple command-line Digital Clock built in C that displays the current system time in real-time directly inside the terminal. This project was created to practice working with time-related functions, loops, terminal manipulation, and basic user interface design in C.

Features-
- Real-time clock updates
- Displays current hours, minutes, and seconds
- Clean terminal-based interface
- Cross-session time synchronization with system clock
- Lightweight and fast

Concepts Used-
- Time and Date Functions (`time.h`)
- Structures (`struct tm`)
- Infinite Loops
- Functions
- Terminal Screen Refreshing
- Formatting Output (`printf`)

Author-
Aishik Ghosh
